About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our Energy &amp; Resources, Utilities team are looking for Summer Interns to join the team.

What you will be doing

You will be joining a team of trusted and well-known experts&nbsp;working with clients&nbsp;in the&nbsp;utilities&nbsp;industry.&nbsp;We collaborate alongside our clients to solve some of their most pressing challenges related to grid reliability,&nbsp;customer&nbsp;affordability,&nbsp;and decarbonization.&nbsp; &nbsp;

You will be supporting the consulting team and our clients on engagements&nbsp;such as: &nbsp;

• Conduct vulnerability&nbsp;studies to forecast the&nbsp;financial impact&nbsp;to transmission &amp; distribution assets from the physical risks of climate change (e.g., flood, wind, heat, wildfires) and develop resilience adaptation plans to mitigate those risks&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Coordinate development of solar and storage assets in low-income communities to enhance grid reliability and generate cost savings for consumers &nbsp;

• Support regulators and utilities to improve distributed energy resources integration and quantify the full benefit stack of microgrids and behind-the-meter assets&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Support asset owners and policymakers to shape the future of the US energy market and the roles of energy networks in enabling and delivering their net zero targets&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Shape the strategic digital roadmap, leading vendor selection and the design and delivery of leading network management and grid optimization solutions (e.g., ADMS, DERMS, advanced planning tools, etc.) for transmission and distribution companies&nbsp; &nbsp;

By the end of the internship, you will gain a strong understanding of&nbsp;the&nbsp;key challenges facing the electricity grid and how utilities&nbsp;operate&nbsp;within&nbsp;their&nbsp;regulatory,&nbsp;technological,&nbsp;and&nbsp;financial&nbsp;context.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;

What are we looking for

We are looking to hire motivated Summer Interns who are deeply interested and curious about the energy industry and who want to develop into industry experts. The ideal candidate will be passionate about energy and will want to gain expertise in this complex industry to provide answers and solutions during interesting and challenging client engagements. &nbsp;

Are you motivated to help&nbsp;utilities&nbsp;solve complex problems and pursue new strategies and opportunities? If the answer is yes, then we are interested in talking to you! &nbsp;

